## Summary

I shipped a production-polished, Apple-idiomatic **`Drawer`** modal surface at parity with `web/src/components/ui/Drawer.tsx`, committed as `192c082a2`.

**Surface** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/Drawer.*`, 8 files, 1520 LOC):
- `Drawer.swift` — edge-anchored glass panel over a tap-to-dismiss scrim; slide+fade (Reduce-Motion-safe); `.isModal` + AccessibilityFocus; Escape via `.cancelAction`.
- `Drawer.Adapter.swift` — Foundation-only projector: `DrawerEdge(web:)` (`side` left/right→leading/trailing, `right` fallback), phase resolution (cached rows kept during reload), VoiceOver summary.
- `Drawer.Model.swift` / `Drawer.Telemetry.swift` — P1/S8 `DrawerSource` seam + `@Observable` model (present/dismiss=`onClose`, stale auto-refresh, offline cache, retry), P1/S10 `DrawerStrings` facade, P1/S11 `view.opened`.
- `Drawer.Views.swift` — scrim, header (title + freshness chip + close), connectivity banner, and **all states** (loading/empty/error/content/footer).
- `Drawer.Previews.swift`, `Drawer.strings`, `Drawer.Tests.swift` (26 XCTest cases).

**Verification (all run on this macOS host, evidence in the log):**
- `swiftformat --lint` **0** · `swiftlint --strict` **0 violations** · placeholder gate **COUNT=0**
- Real-SDK `swiftc -typecheck` **iOS 18 + macOS 15** → both EXIT=0
- Isolated SwiftPM build + **26/26 tests** pass (Swift 6 strict concurrency)
- `xcodegen generate` enumerates all 8 files into both app targets
- Built `Shared.xcframework` (16m) and **ran the full-app `xcodebuild`** (iOS-Sim + macOS): both EXIT=65, **RED only** on the pre-existing `AIRestorePanel.Tests.swift` XCTest-in-app issue — **zero Drawer errors**, `Drawer.strings` copied into both bundles.

**Necessary wiring** (ToolCard precedent, enumerated — not silent): added `TeslaSync/modals-dialogs` to `project.yml` (both targets) + `.swiftlint.yml`, plus a `macos-pending-verifications.md` row for the P99 signed gate. The log ends `EXIT=0 / STATUS=DONE`. Pre-existing dirty files were left untouched.

